st+=sec('5. Likely panel questions and suggested answers')
qas=[('What is the main purpose of DaGOAL?','DaGoal is a gamified daily activity planner intended to help users reduce excessive screen time by replacing passive digital consumption with physical, mental, and creative activities. It uses preference-informed quests, flexible choices, progress feedback, and rewards to encourage participation.'),('What problem are you trying to address?','The capstone focuses on excessive screen use and passive routines, particularly among students and young adults. DaGoal offers structured real-world activities as alternatives and optional screen-avoidance quests. Our evaluation measures initial user perceptions after a short trial, not a causal or long-term reduction in screen time.'),('Who are the target users?','The manuscript identifies students and young adults as the intended audience. In the evaluation, respondents were reported as ages 19-26. The Android implementation supports Android API 29 and later; that device requirement is separate from the research population.'),('How does DaGOAL differ from a basic to-do list?','It combines task tracking with XP, gold, levels, streaks, achievements, avatar customization, inventory, and a shop. It also has optional device-assisted step tracking and app-avoidance quest monitoring. Comparative effectiveness must be supported by study data.'),('How are daily quests generated?','TaskManager creates a date-specific set using templates and user preference/profile signals, preserves due recurring custom quests, considers level-based quest slots, and may add an avoidance quest when apps were selected. Some choices are randomized.'),('How are quests tracked?','Generic quests use manual confirmation; count/repetition goals update stored progress; supported walking goals use Android step sensors when permission and hardware are available; timed screen-avoidance quests are started by the user and rely on Usage Access plus overlay permission for interruption UI.'),('How does a user earn XP and gold?','Each quest stores reward values. On completion, TaskManager applies eligible active boosts, adds XP and gold to the local user record, evaluates level thresholds, and updates achievements/reward counters.'),('Why did you use gamification?','The design uses feedback and progression mechanics to make completion visible and give users in-app incentives. That is our design rationale. Whether it increases adherence or motivation is a research question answered only by our evaluation results.'),('Where is data stored?','Most structured app state is local in SQLite, with UI/onboarding preferences in SharedPreferences. Firebase Authentication handles account identity, while Firestore is used for selected profile/avatar/streak and online features. It is a hybrid design; not every record is cloud-synchronized.'),('Can it work offline?','Many core quest and progression operations are local, so they can work without network once set up. Authentication, cloud synchronization, and online shop functions depend on connectivity. Demonstrate exact offline behavior on the defense build.'),('How do you protect privacy for app monitoring?','Monitoring is tied to an avoidance quest that the user starts and requires Android Usage Access; interruption overlays require overlay permission. The app uses a foreground service notification while monitoring. State the exact policy and data handling commitments from your approved privacy documentation.'),('The manuscript says blocking. Does the current build hard-block selected apps?','The current code monitors recent foreground app usage during a user-started avoidance quest and presents an overlay with a go-home action or timed ignore/reset options. Describe this observed implementation accurately; do not promise guaranteed OS-level blocking.'),('What if permission is denied or no step sensor exists?','The permission-dependent feature cannot fully operate. Step tracking needs a compatible sensor and activity-recognition permission. Avoidance monitoring needs Usage Access, and overlay presentation needs overlay permission. Other quest functions remain available; demonstrate the denied state on your build.'),('How is streak calculated?','The app stores current streak, last completion date, longest streak, and streak history. TaskManager checks date transitions around daily quest generation/completion and updates streak state. Explain the qualifying rule from verified current behavior and demonstrate a scenario.'),('What are the main screens?','DashboardActivity is the main workspace and hosts Quest, Wardrobe, Shop, and Me. Onboarding/authentication, avatar creation, profiling, app selection, daily reveal, streak details, and settings use separate Activities.'),('What limitations did you identify?','Some features depend on Android permissions and sensors, selected cloud features require connectivity, and generated quests may vary. The current database upgrade path drops and recreates daily_tasks and task_templates, so preserving those records through migration is an important future improvement.'),('How did you functionally test the application?','The manuscript reports 97 manual functional test cases covering startup/authentication, offline use, onboarding, quest generation and replacement, task verification, rewards, shop/wardrobe, profile/streaks, permissions, synchronization, step tracking, and avoidance behavior. All 97 were marked Passed under the documented test conditions. This is functional testing, not proof of long-term behavior change.'),('How did you evaluate user perceptions?','Respondents used the app for three days, then completed an online software-quality questionnaire using a four-point agreement scale across usability, enjoyment/engagement, screen-time management, performance, and overall experience. The manuscript reports n=57 in the abstract/table, but its implementation-results text says 56 participants; reconcile the correct number before defense.'),('What were the evaluation results?','The reported grand mean was 3.31 (SD=0.30), interpreted as Strongly Agree. Domain means: Usability 3.42 (SD .39, Strongly Agree); Enjoyment/Engagement 3.22 (.46, Agree); Screen Time Management 3.40 (.38, Strongly Agree); Performance 3.25 (.40, Agree); Overall Experience 3.26 (.41, Strongly Agree). These are respondent ratings, not objective usage-time measurements.'),('Can you conclude that DaGoal reduced screen time?','Not definitively from this evaluation. The study lasted three days and relied mainly on participant feedback. The screen-time domain mean (3.40) indicates respondents felt the app raised awareness or encouraged better habits; it is not a measured before-and-after reduction or evidence of sustained effect.'),('What sample-count issue should the team clarify?','The abstract and results table label the evaluation n=57, while the implementation-results paragraph says findings were based on 56 participants. Check the raw response export and final analyzed dataset, then correct the manuscript or explain exclusions and state the valid n consistently.'),('What is the most important contribution?','The contribution is [exact manuscript wording]. In the software, it is embodied in [specific capability]. We avoid claiming novelty beyond what our related-work review supports.'),('What would you improve next?','Priorities include safer non-destructive SQLite migrations, clearer permission fallback handling, broader device testing, and evaluation with intended users. Improvements should follow measured findings and participant feedback.'),('What if you do not know an answer?','“I want to be precise. I can confirm [known fact]. The detail is not in the evidence I have at hand, so I would verify it against [code/manuscript/test record] rather than guess.”')]
for q,a in qas: st+=qa(q,a)
st += [PageBreak()]

st+=sec('6. Study design, reported results, and what they mean')
st += [P('Evaluation procedure','H2x'),P('The manuscript reports distributing the APK to selected respondents, who used it for three days. They then completed an online software-quality questionnaire using a four-point scale (1 = Strongly Disagree to 4 = Strongly Agree). The evaluated domains were Usability, Enjoyment and Engagement, Screen Time Management, Performance, and Overall Experience.'),P('Functional testing','H2x'),P('The project reports 97 manual functional test cases, all marked Passed under the conditions used. Coverage included startup/account flows, offline access, onboarding, quest generation/replacement, manual/count/timed/step verification, rewards, shop and wardrobe, settings, permissions, sync, and background tracking. Present this as a test result, not proof that every device/environment is defect-free.'),P('User evaluation results from the capstone print copy','H2x')]
result_rows=[[P('Domain','TH'),P('Mean','TH'),P('SD','TH'),P('Interpretation','TH')],[P('Usability','TB'),P('3.42','TB'),P('0.39','TB'),P('Strongly Agree','TB')],[P('Enjoyment and Engagement','TB'),P('3.22','TB'),P('0.46','TB'),P('Agree','TB')],[P('Screen Time Management','TB'),P('3.40','TB'),P('0.38','TB'),P('Strongly Agree','TB')],[P('Performance','TB'),P('3.25','TB'),P('0.40','TB'),P('Agree','TB')],[P('Overall Experience','TB'),P('3.26','TB'),P('0.41','TB'),P('Strongly Agree','TB')],[P('Grand Mean','TB'),P('3.31','TB'),P('0.30','TB'),P('Strongly Agree','TB')]]
st += [make_table(result_rows,[2.55*inch,.85*inch,.75*inch,2.15*inch]),P('Interpretation to use at defense','H2x'),P('“The results indicate positive initial acceptance and perceived usability after the three-day trial. Respondents gave Screen Time Management a 3.40 mean, suggesting they felt the app increased awareness or encouraged better habits. Because the study period was short and the measure was self-reported, we cannot conclude that screen time objectively decreased or that the effect persisted.”','Callout'),P('Important manuscript consistency check','H2x'),P('The abstract and table identify n=57, while the implementation-results paragraph states 56 participants. Confirm the correct analyzed sample using the raw response export and explain any exclusions. Use one consistent n in the defense slides and oral answer.','Callout'),PageBreak()]

st+=sec('7. Technical and methodological limits to explain clearly','These are points to prepare for, not reasons to undermine the project. A measured, specific answer usually builds more confidence than an absolute claim.')
limits=[('Android permission dependence','Activity recognition, Usage Access, overlay, and notification behavior varies by OS version/device settings. State the permission and feature dependency.'),('Sensor availability','Step tracking requires a compatible step counter/detector. Explain what your test devices supported.'),('Hybrid persistence','The app primarily uses local SQLite; selected cloud features use Firebase. Do not imply complete backup/sync unless your build and tests demonstrate it.'),('Database migration','DatabaseHelper.onUpgrade drops and recreates daily_tasks and task_templates. Existing quest/template records can be lost during upgrade; a preserving migration should be prioritized.'),('Monitoring semantics','Avoidance monitoring checks foreground app usage through Android UsageStats and may interrupt with an overlay. It is not a guaranteed hard block and can be affected by permissions/background restrictions/device behavior.'),('Efficacy vs implementation','A working feature demonstrates implementation. It does not prove better habits, health, productivity, or sustained behavior.'),('Research specifics','Population, sampling, instrument validity, response rate, evaluation method, and numerical findings must come from approved research documents.')]
rows=[[P('Topic','TH'),P('Accurate framing','TH')]]+[[P(a,'TB'),P(b,'TB')] for a,b in limits]
st += [make_table(rows,[1.5*inch,4.8*inch]),P('Polished limitation answer','H2x'),P('“One technical limitation is that some features depend on Android-level permissions and supported sensors, so behavior can vary by device. Our core quest state is mainly stored locally, while only selected account/profile and online functions use Firebase. We also identified that the current database upgrade path recreates daily quests and templates, so preserving these records through migration is a priority for future work.”','Callout'),PageBreak()]

